---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="CLI commands"
  description="Use clink for discovery, directory approval and one-shot generation. It installs alongside the separate clink-mcp-server command."
  toc={[
    ["discover", "Inspect capabilities"],
    ["allow", "Approve a directory"],
    ["generate", "Generate"],
    ["consumer", "Bind application configuration"],
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="discover">Inspect capabilities</h2>
  <Code label="Terminal" code="clink generation-capabilities --json" />
  <p>
    Read the supported schemas and family records without starting an agent or
    signing in. Each record includes executable names, model selection kinds and
    verification information. The optional executable check hashes a particular
    regular file without running it. Supply the agent name and absolute
    executable path together.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="Terminal · replace the executable path"
    code="clink generation-capabilities --json --cli codex --executable /absolute/path/to/codex"
  />
  <p>
    Inspect <code>preflight.status</code> for <code>compatible</code>,{" "}
    <code>missing</code>, <code>invalid_executable</code> or{" "}
    <code>admission_unverified</code>. Authentication and model entitlement are
    evaluated during a real request.{" "}
    <a href="/reference/#admissions">Operation-specific compatibility</a>.
  </p>
  <h2 id="allow">Approve a directory</h2>
  <p>
    From the intended project, approve a folder for one configured client. Clink
    resolves its canonical path, asks once and defaults to No. A saved root
    covers descendants. Selecting a broad root, such as your home, expands what
    the client can target.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="Terminal · interactive approval"
    code={'clink allow "$(pwd -P)" --cli codex'}
  />
  <p>
    <code>--yes</code> is explicit consent for scripts. Use <code>--json</code>{" "}
    to get a machine-readable grant receipt. Inspect <code>status</code>,{" "}
    <code>grant_saved</code> and <code>error_code</code>. A user declining a
    terminal prompt can exit cleanly without saving a grant.
  </p>
  <Code
    label="Terminal · explicitly grant the chosen project"
    code={'clink allow "$(pwd -P)" --cli codex --yes --json'}
  />
  <p>
    Use <code>--project /absolute/bound/project</code> to reproduce an MCP
    server’s configuration when granting a root. Restart that server to load
    changes. Release 0.2.3 can offer interactive directory approval during
    eligible terminal generation and then continue the same request. A headless
    caller enrolls the directory in advance.
  </p>
  <h2 id="generate">Generate</h2>
  <Code
    label="Terminal"
    code="clink generate --request-json - < request.json"
  />
  <p>
    Close stdin after one UTF-8 JSON object. The command returns one terminal
    result on stdout and writes diagnostics to stderr. Supply instructions and
    source text in the JSON fields. Use the{" "}
    <a href="/cli/generation/">request and result guide</a> for a complete
    invocation and error handling.
  </p>
  <h2 id="consumer">Bind application configuration</h2>
  <Code
    label="Terminal · app-managed configuration"
    code={
      "clink --consumer-config-dir /absolute/canonical/app-config generate --request-json - < request.json"
    }
  />
  <p>
    An application can bind an existing, canonical configuration directory
    before reading a generation request. This source is independent of ordinary
    manifests. Bootstrap an appropriate consumer manifest first, then bind the
    same directory for <code>allow</code> and <code>generate</code>. The{" "}
    <code>allow</code> command accepts either this binding or{" "}
    <code>--project</code>.{" "}
    <a href="/configuration/#consumer">Consumer manifest example</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>clink --help</code> and <code>clink COMMAND --help</code> print the
    installed syntax.
  </p>
</Docs>
